# Shrimp Tacos

Based on [http://www.yummly.co/recipe/…](http://www.yummly.co/recipe/Honey-Lime-Shrimp-Tacos-1576139) (wayback unavailable)

{ rating="4" image="shrimp_tacos.jpg" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

### Shrimp

- [ ] 1 lb [shrimp]{ ing="shrimp" }, peeled
- [ ] 1/4 cup [olive oil]{ ing="olive-oil" }
- [ ] 2.5 Tbsp [honey]{ ing="honey" }
- [ ] 1 [lime]{ ing="lime" }, juiced
- [ ] 3 cloves [garlic]{ ing="garlic" }
- [ ] (Optional) small slice of a jalapeño or pinch of [red pepper flakes]{ ing="red-pepper-flakes" }
- [ ] 1/2 tsp each of [salt & pepper]{ ing="salt-pepper" }

### Tacos

- [ ] [Hard corn]{ ing="hard-corn" } or soft flour tacos, toasted
- [ ] [Avocado]{ ing="avocado" }
- [ ] [Salsa]{ ing="salsa" }
- [ ] [Shredded Lettuce]{ ing="shredded-lettuce" }
- [ ] [Jalapeño]{ ing="jalapeno" }, sliced
- [ ] [Rice]{ ing="rice" }
- [ ] [Diced onion]{ ing="diced-onion" }, tomato, etc.

## Recipe

1. Whisk together the [olive oil]{ ing="olive-oil" }, [honey]{ ing="honey" }, [lime]{ ing="lime" } juice, [garlic]{ ing="garlic" }, salt, and [pepper]{ ing="salt-pepper" }
1. Simmer the sauce in a sauce pan for a few minutes, then add the [shrimp]{ ing="shrimp" }
1. Cook [shrimp]{ ing="shrimp" } on one side until pink, then flip, and cook until just pink all over (~6 min)
